


Logical: IdentityAssertion
Id: identity-assertion
Title: "Identity Assertion"
Description: """
A representation of asserted identity information, including names, postal addresses, and phone numbers with their validity periods.

- Informed by [TEFCA IAS SOP](https://rce.sequoiaproject.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/XP-Implementation-SOP-IAS.pdf)
- Informed by FHIR [Patient resource](https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/patient.html)
- Informed by US-Core [Patient Profile](https://build.fhir.org/ig/HL7/US-Core/StructureDefinition-us-core-patient.html)
"""

* masterIdentifier 1..1 string "The master identifier"
* masterIdentifier.system 1..1 string "The system of the master identifier"
* masterIdentifier.value 1..1 string "The identifier value"

* names 1..* BackboneElement "The person's names"
* names.first 1..1 string "The first name"
* names.middle 0..* string "The middle names"
* names.last 1..1 string "The last name"
* names.prefix 0..1 string "The prefix"
* names.suffix 0..1 string "The suffix"
* names.validityPeriod 0..1 Period "The validity of this name"

* addresses 0..* Address "Physical addresses"
* addresses.period 0..1 Period "The validity of this address"
* addresses.use 0..1 code "home | work | temp | old | billing"
* addresses.type 0..1 code "postal | physical | both"
* addresses.line 0..* string "The street address"
* addresses.city 1..1 string "The city of the address"
* addresses.state 1..1 string "The state of the address"
* addresses.postalCode 0..1 string "The postal code"
* addresses.country 0..1 string "The country of the address"


* phoneNumbers 0..* BackboneElement "Phone numbers"
* phoneNumbers.number 1..1 string "The phone number"
* phoneNumbers.validityPeriod 0..1 Period "The validity of this number"
* phoneNumbers.type 0..1 code "phone | fax | pager | url | sms | other"
* phoneNumbers.use 0..1 code "home | work | temp | old | mobile"
* phoneNumbers.rank 0..1 integer "Specify preferred order of use (1 = highest)"

* emails 0..* BackboneElement "Email addresses or direct messaging"
* emails.address 1..1 string "The email address"
* emails.validityPeriod 0..1 Period "The validity of this email"
* emails.type 0..1 code "work | personal"

* ssn 0..* string "The social security number"

* identifiers 0..* BackboneElement "Correlated external Identifiers"
* identifiers.value 1..1 string "The identifier value"
* identifiers.system 0..1 string "The identifier system URL"
* identifiers.type 0..1 code "The identifier type"
* identifiers.validityPeriod 0..1 Period "The validity of this identifier"
* identifiers.issuer 0..1 string "The issuer of this identifier"

* birthDate 0..1 date "The birth date"

* photo 0..1 Attachment "The person's photo"

* gender 0..1 code "male | female | other | unknown"

* maritalStatus 0..1 code "unmarried | married | annulled | divorced"

* race 0..1 code "Asked but unknown | Asked but declined | unknown | American Indian | Asian | Black | Native Hawaiian | White | Other"
* ethnicity 0..1 code "The ethnicity of the person"
* tribalAffiliation 0..1 code "Tribal affiliation"
* religion 0..1 code "The religion of the person"

* placeOfBirth 0..1 string "The place of birth"

* placeOfDeath 0..1 string "The place of death"
* deathDate 0..1 date "The date of death"   
* causeOfDeath 0..1 code "The cause of death"

* assuranceLevel 0..1 code "The level of assurance"
* verificationStatus 0..1 code "The verification status"
* assuranceDate 0..1 date "The date of assurance"
* assuranceMethod 0..1 code "The method of assurance"

* contact 0..* BackboneElement "Emergency contacts"
* contact.relationship 0..1 code "Relationship to the person"
* contact.name 0..1 string "Name of contact"
* contact.phone 0..1 string "Phone of contact"
* contact.email 0..1 string "Email of contact"
* contact.address 0..1 string "Address of contact"
* contact.gender 0..1 code "Gender of contact"
* contact.period 0..1 Period "Contact period"

* communication 0..* BackboneElement "Languages spoken"
* communication.language 0..1 code "Language"
* communication.preferred 0..1 boolean "Preferred language"

* generalPractitioner 0..* BackboneElement "General practitioners"
* managingOrganization 0..1 string "Managing organization"  


Mapping: IdentityAssertionToPatient
Id: identity-assertion-to-patient
Title: "Identity Assertion to FHIR Patient"
Description: "Informative mapping from IdentityAssertion elements to corresponding FHIR R4 Patient elements. Fields without a Patient element or standard extension are not mapped."
Source: IdentityAssertion
Target: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/Patient"
* -> "Patient"
* masterIdentifier -> "Patient.identifier"
* masterIdentifier.system -> "Patient.identifier.system"
* masterIdentifier.value -> "Patient.identifier.value"
* names -> "Patient.name"
* names.first -> "Patient.name.given" "Map as a given name."
* names.middle -> "Patient.name.given" "Map additional given names in order."
* names.last -> "Patient.name.family"
* names.prefix -> "Patient.name.prefix"
* names.suffix -> "Patient.name.suffix"
* names.validityPeriod -> "Patient.name.period"
* addresses -> "Patient.address"
* addresses.period -> "Patient.address.period"
* addresses.use -> "Patient.address.use"
* addresses.type -> "Patient.address.type"
* addresses.line -> "Patient.address.line"
* addresses.city -> "Patient.address.city"
* addresses.state -> "Patient.address.state"
* addresses.postalCode -> "Patient.address.postalCode"
* addresses.country -> "Patient.address.country"
* phoneNumbers -> "Patient.telecom"
* phoneNumbers.number -> "Patient.telecom.value"
* phoneNumbers.type -> "Patient.telecom.system"
* phoneNumbers.use -> "Patient.telecom.use"
* phoneNumbers.rank -> "Patient.telecom.rank"
* phoneNumbers.validityPeriod -> "Patient.telecom.period"
* emails -> "Patient.telecom"
* emails.address -> "Patient.telecom.value"
* emails.validityPeriod -> "Patient.telecom.period"
* emails.type -> "Patient.telecom.use" "The personal code requires interpretation, such as mapping to home."
* ssn -> "Patient.identifier.value" "Represent each value as an identifier and supply an appropriate system and type."
* identifiers -> "Patient.identifier"
* identifiers.value -> "Patient.identifier.value"
* identifiers.system -> "Patient.identifier.system"
* identifiers.type -> "Patient.identifier.type"
* identifiers.validityPeriod -> "Patient.identifier.period"
* identifiers.issuer -> "Patient.identifier.assigner.display" "Convert the issuer string to an Identifier.assigner reference when possible."
* birthDate -> "Patient.birthDate"
* photo -> "Patient.photo"
* gender -> "Patient.gender"
* maritalStatus -> "Patient.maritalStatus"
* race -> "Patient.extension[http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-race]"
* ethnicity -> "Patient.extension[http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-ethnicity]"
* placeOfBirth -> "Patient.extension[http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/patient-birthPlace]" "Convert the string to the extension's valueAddress."
* deathDate -> "Patient.deceasedDateTime"
* contact -> "Patient.contact"
* contact.relationship -> "Patient.contact.relationship"
* contact.name -> "Patient.contact.name.text"
* contact.phone -> "Patient.contact.telecom.value" "Set ContactPoint.system to phone."
* contact.email -> "Patient.contact.telecom.value" "Set ContactPoint.system to email."
* contact.address -> "Patient.contact.address.text"
* contact.gender -> "Patient.contact.gender"
* contact.period -> "Patient.contact.period"
* communication -> "Patient.communication"
* communication.language -> "Patient.communication.language"
* communication.preferred -> "Patient.communication.preferred"
* generalPractitioner -> "Patient.generalPractitioner"
* managingOrganization -> "Patient.managingOrganization" "Convert the organization string to a Reference(Organization)."

Logical: OIDCToken
Id: oidc-token
Title: "OpenID Connect ID Token"
Description: """
A logical representation of common JWT registered claims, OpenID Connect ID Token claims, and the OIDC for Identity Assurance `verified_claims` object. It is not a JWT wire-format or signature model. See [RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519), [OpenID Connect Core](https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html), and [OpenID Connect for Identity Assurance](https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-4-identity-assurance-1_0.html).
"""

* iss 1..1 uri "Issuer"
* sub 1..1 string "Subject identifier"
* aud 1..* string "Audience identifiers"
* exp 1..1 decimal "Expiration time as a JWT NumericDate"
* iat 1..1 decimal "Issued-at time as a JWT NumericDate"
* nbf 0..1 decimal "Not-before time as a JWT NumericDate"
* jti 0..1 string "JWT identifier"

* auth_time 0..1 decimal "Time of end-user authentication as a JWT NumericDate"
* nonce 0..1 string "Nonce supplied by the relying party"
* acr 0..1 string "Authentication context class reference"
* amr 0..* string "Authentication methods used"
* azp 0..1 string "Authorized party"
* at_hash 0..1 string "Access token hash"
* c_hash 0..1 string "Authorization code hash"

* name 0..1 string "Full name"
* given_name 0..1 string "Given name"
* middle_name 0..1 string "Middle name(s)"
* family_name 0..1 string "Family name"
* nickname 0..1 string "Casual name"
* preferred_username 0..1 string "Preferred username"
* profile 0..1 uri "Profile page URL"
* picture 0..1 uri "Profile picture URL"
* website 0..1 uri "Web page URL"
* email 0..1 string "Email address"
* email_verified 0..1 boolean "Whether the email address was verified"
* gender 0..1 string "Gender"
* birthdate 0..1 date "Birth date"
* zoneinfo 0..1 string "Time zone"
* locale 0..1 string "Locale"
* phone_number 0..1 string "Phone number"
* phone_number_verified 0..1 boolean "Whether the phone number was verified"
* address 0..1 BackboneElement "Postal address"
* address.formatted 0..1 string "Full formatted address"
* address.street_address 0..1 string "Street address"
* address.locality 0..1 string "City or locality"
* address.region 0..1 string "State, province, or region"
* address.postal_code 0..1 string "Postal code"
* address.country 0..1 string "Country"
* updated_at 0..1 decimal "Time the end-user information was last updated as a JWT NumericDate"

* verified_claims 0..* BackboneElement "Verified claims with their verification context"
* verified_claims.verification 0..1 BackboneElement "Verification context"
* verified_claims.verification.trust_framework 0..1 string "Trust framework"
* verified_claims.verification.time 0..1 dateTime "Time of verification"
* verified_claims.verification.assurance_level 0..1 string "Assurance level"
* verified_claims.claims 0..1 BackboneElement "Identity claims covered by the verification"
* verified_claims.claims.given_name 0..1 string "Verified given name"
* verified_claims.claims.middle_name 0..1 string "Verified middle name(s)"
* verified_claims.claims.family_name 0..1 string "Verified family name"
* verified_claims.claims.birthdate 0..1 date "Verified birth date"
* verified_claims.claims.email 0..1 string "Verified email address"
* verified_claims.claims.phone_number 0..1 string "Verified phone number"
* verified_claims.claims.ssn_last4 0..1 string "Proposal-specific claim for the last four SSN digits"

Mapping: IdentityAssertionToOIDCToken
Id: identity-assertion-to-oidc-token
Title: "Identity Assertion to OpenID Connect ID Token"
Description: "Informative mapping from identity attributes to the local OIDCToken logical model. Registered JWT claims are represented by OIDCToken but are token-issuance metadata and are not derived from IdentityAssertion."
Source: IdentityAssertion
Target: "http://hl7.org/fhir/us/identity-matching/StructureDefinition/oidc-token"
* -> "OIDCToken"
* masterIdentifier.value -> "OIDCToken.sub" "Use only when this is the subject identifier assigned for this issuer and relying-party context."
* names.first -> "OIDCToken.given_name"
* names.middle -> "OIDCToken.middle_name"
* names.last -> "OIDCToken.family_name"
* addresses -> "OIDCToken.address" "OIDC models one address object; select the applicable current address."
* addresses.line -> "OIDCToken.address.street_address"
* addresses.city -> "OIDCToken.address.locality"
* addresses.state -> "OIDCToken.address.region"
* addresses.postalCode -> "OIDCToken.address.postal_code"
* addresses.country -> "OIDCToken.address.country"
* phoneNumbers.number -> "OIDCToken.phone_number" "OIDC models one phone_number claim; select the applicable current number."
* emails.address -> "OIDCToken.email" "OIDC models one email claim; select the applicable current address."
* birthDate -> "OIDCToken.birthdate"
* photo -> "OIDCToken.picture" "Convert to a retrievable image URL when available."
* gender -> "OIDCToken.gender"
* ssn -> "OIDCToken.verified_claims.claims.ssn_last4" "Only derive and disclose the last four digits when authorized; never map the full SSN. This is a proposal-specific claim, not a standard OIDC claim."
* assuranceLevel -> "OIDCToken.verified_claims.verification.assurance_level" "Map to the OIDC4IDA verification assurance level."
* assuranceDate -> "OIDCToken.verified_claims.verification.time" "Map to the time of identity verification."

Mapping: OIDCTokenToIdentityAssertion
Id: oidc-token-to-identity-assertion
Title: "OpenID Connect ID Token to Identity Assertion"
Description: "Informative reverse mapping from the local OIDCToken logical model to IdentityAssertion. OIDC claims are often singular while IdentityAssertion permits repetitions, and the verified_claims values should be preferred over corresponding unverified top-level claims when present. JWT issuance metadata and claims without an IdentityAssertion equivalent are not mapped."
Source: OIDCToken
Target: "http://hl7.org/fhir/us/identity-matching/StructureDefinition/identity-assertion"
* -> "IdentityAssertion"
* iss -> "IdentityAssertion.masterIdentifier.system" "Use as the identifier system only when this is the namespace for sub."
* sub -> "IdentityAssertion.masterIdentifier.value"
* given_name -> "IdentityAssertion.names.first"
* middle_name -> "IdentityAssertion.names.middle"
* family_name -> "IdentityAssertion.names.last"
* verified_claims.claims.given_name -> "IdentityAssertion.names.first" "Prefer this verified value over given_name when both are present."
* verified_claims.claims.middle_name -> "IdentityAssertion.names.middle" "Prefer this verified value over middle_name when both are present."
* verified_claims.claims.family_name -> "IdentityAssertion.names.last" "Prefer this verified value over family_name when both are present."
* address -> "IdentityAssertion.addresses" "OIDC carries one address object; IdentityAssertion permits multiple addresses."
* address.street_address -> "IdentityAssertion.addresses.line" "Split into lines when needed."
* address.locality -> "IdentityAssertion.addresses.city"
* address.region -> "IdentityAssertion.addresses.state"
* address.postal_code -> "IdentityAssertion.addresses.postalCode"
* address.country -> "IdentityAssertion.addresses.country"
* phone_number -> "IdentityAssertion.phoneNumbers.number"
* verified_claims.claims.phone_number -> "IdentityAssertion.phoneNumbers.number" "Prefer this verified value over phone_number when both are present."
* email -> "IdentityAssertion.emails.address"
* verified_claims.claims.email -> "IdentityAssertion.emails.address" "Prefer this verified value over email when both are present."
* birthdate -> "IdentityAssertion.birthDate"
* verified_claims.claims.birthdate -> "IdentityAssertion.birthDate" "Prefer this verified value over birthdate when both are present."
* picture -> "IdentityAssertion.photo.url" "Convert the URI to an Attachment URL."
* gender -> "IdentityAssertion.gender"
* verified_claims.verification.assurance_level -> "IdentityAssertion.assuranceLevel"
* verified_claims.verification.time -> "IdentityAssertion.assuranceDate"


Mapping: IdentityAssertionToOORECR
Id: identity-assertion-to-oor-ecr
Title: "Identity Assertion to Person-Bearing OOR/ECR vLEI Credential"
Description: """
Informative mapping to the person-bearing OOR/ECR credential attributes shown in GLEIF's vLEI technical examples. GLEIF describes vLEI as combining the legal entity, an individual's identity, and their organizational role ([vLEI overview](https://www.gleif.org/en/organizational-identity/lei-vlei/the-verifiable-lei-vlei)). The OOR/ECR examples use `LEI` and `personLegalName`, with `officialRole` for OOR and `engagementContextRole` for ECR ([GLEIF vLEI trust-chain examples](https://github.com/GLEIF-IT/vlei-trainings/blob/main/markdown/103_10_vLEI_Trust_Chain.md); [QVI issuance workflow](https://github.com/GLEIF-IT/qvi-software/blob/main/qvi-workflow/kli_only/vlei-workflow.sh)).

The exact credential schema is identified and validated using its SAID. This mapping uses the example attribute names and is not a substitute for resolving and validating the issued OOR/ECR credential. IdentityAssertion has no organizational-role or engagement-context element, so those credential attributes are not mapped.
"""
Source: IdentityAssertion
Target: "https://github.com/GLEIF-IT/vlei-trainings/blob/main/markdown/103_10_vLEI_Trust_Chain.md"
* -> "OOR/ECR credential attributes"
* names -> "personLegalName" "Use the current legal name; the credential attribute is a single full-name string, not separate given and family name fields."
* masterIdentifier.value -> "credential issuee AID" "Map only when this is the same AID used as the credential issuee; the AID is the credential subject binding, not a personLegalName attribute."
* identifiers.value -> "LEI" "Map only when this identifier is the represented organization's LEI, not an identifier of the individual."

